    {
      "id": "0e5efa7a-facf-4fa3-b2f0-580552ebbb45",
      "name": "Start here",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.stickyNote",
      "position": [
        0,
        0
      ],
      "parameters": {
        "color": 4,
        "width": 560,
        "height": 440,
        "content": "## Start here\n\nAssemble a materials evidence packet for an AOG request. Each serialized part is checked against three source systems, then routed to an MRO reservation or quarantine record.\n\nFor materials controllers and maintenance support teams. This workflow does not certify airworthiness or authorize installation. A qualified person must review the evidence before operational use."
      },
      "typeVersion": 1
    },
    {
      "id": "a33ec8b0-cc0d-48e3-8f9b-a2efe9c473c1",
      "name": "Connect and configure",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.stickyNote",
      "position": [
        0,
        512
      ],
      "parameters": {
        "color": 5,
        "width": 560,
        "height": 444,
        "content": "## Connect and configure\n\n1. Select a Header Auth credential on the intake webhook. Call it from a trusted server.\n2. Replace the OEM, life-history, directive and MRO example URLs. Select Header Auth credentials for each service.\n3. Every lookup must return partNumber and serialNumber. OEM also returns boolean oemEligible; life history returns releaseCertificate and numeric remainingCycles; directive status returns boolean openDirective.\n4. Connect OpenAI, Google Drive and Telegram. Choose the archive folder and controller chat.\n5. POST requestId, aircraftId and a non-empty parts array. Every part needs partNumber and serialNumber.\n\nUse sandbox MRO endpoints for the first run. Example domains are placeholders, not included services."
      },
      "typeVersion": 1
    },
    {
      "id": "e0c55af4-2617-4d8c-868c-20e3bd9d85b7",
      "name": "Before switching on",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.stickyNote",
      "position": [
        16,
        1024
      ],
      "parameters": {
        "color": 3,
        "width": 560,
        "height": 420,
        "content": "## Before switching on\n\nTry an eligible part, a missing certificate, an unknown directive status and two different serial numbers in one request. Missing evidence must go to quarantine.\n\nService errors stop the run. GET lookups retry up to three attempts; external writes are not automatically retried. Inspect successful writes before rerunning a failed execution to avoid duplicate reservations or notifications.\n\nThe model receives the part evidence. Use only data your organization permits it to process. The workflow stays inactive after import."
      },
      "typeVersion": 1
    },
    {
      "id": "8acdb52d-9af9-4f1a-9be7-df409e388ec3",
      "name": "1. Receive and separate the parts",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.stickyNote",
      "position": [
        640,
        0
      ],
      "parameters": {
        "color": 7,
        "width": 1040,
        "height": 590,
        "content": "## 1. Receive and separate the parts\n\nThe webhook accepts a requestId, aircraftId and parts array. The next two steps reject missing identifiers and duplicate part identities, then create one item per serialized part.\n\nKeep the same requestId when discussing a request with the controller. Authentication is required on the webhook; do not put its secret in a public form."
      },
      "typeVersion": 1
    },
    {
      "id": "c673e58c-bf72-419c-9916-1040ed015e5f",
      "name": "2. Match three evidence sources",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.stickyNote",
      "position": [
        1760,
        0
      ],
      "parameters": {
        "color": 6,
        "width": 1040,
        "height": 820,
        "content": "## 2. Match three evidence sources\n\nEach lookup receives the part number and serial number. The merge waits for all three streams; the following code matches evidence by those identifiers, not by response order.\n\nKeep these response keys unchanged when adapting the API calls. A missing match remains unresolved. Duplicate matches stop the run so two records cannot be mistaken for one."
      },
      "typeVersion": 1
    },
    {
      "id": "e0a3bbec-1042-45dc-883f-466b2abb75a4",
      "name": "3. Calculate blockers, then explain them",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.stickyNote",
      "position": [
        2880,
        0
      ],
      "parameters": {
        "color": 7,
        "width": 1040,
        "height": 820,
        "content": "## 3. Calculate blockers, then explain them\n\nEligibility requires OEM confirmation, a release-certificate reference, a positive numeric remainingCycles value and openDirective set to false. Anything missing stays blocked.\n\nThe model writes an explanation only. Keep Part Decision restores the code's blocker list and releaseState after the model call, so model text cannot choose the route."
      },
      "typeVersion": 1
    },
    {
      "id": "62cfed18-f748-4988-b7c0-9863a66b1692",
      "name": "4. Record the MRO outcome",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.stickyNote",
      "position": [
        4000,
        0
      ],
      "parameters": {
        "color": 6,
        "width": 1040,
        "height": 820,
        "content": "## 4. Record the MRO outcome\n\nThe true branch requests a reservation. The false branch creates a quarantine record. Both are writes to your MRO system; verify the URLs and payloads in a sandbox first.\n\nThe two outcome steps retain the original identifiers and decision alongside the service response. A successful API response is not an installation approval."
      },
      "typeVersion": 1
    },
    {
      "id": "e4b931d2-cdfc-45a9-9110-bf715341d839",
      "name": "5. Save the packet and notify the controller",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.stickyNote",
      "position": [
        5120,
        0
      ],
      "parameters": {
        "color": 7,
        "width": 1040,
        "height": 590,
        "content": "## 5. Save the packet and notify the controller\n\nThe aggregate collects the part decisions. Drive creates a text file containing the JSON packet in your selected folder. Telegram sends the number of parts and saved file ID.\n\nOpen the file during testing and check that every requested serial number appears. The notification runs only after Drive succeeds."
      },
      "typeVersion": 1
    }
  ],
